# Files that exist for the repository, not for the website.
#
# Wrangler uploads wrangler.jsonc's assets.directory minus these entries, using
# .gitignore syntax. _headers is consumed by the platform rather than served,
# so it is not listed.
#
# The deployed site is exactly index.html plus assets/. Everything else here —
# the measurement harness, the corpus, the tests, the docs — is what makes the
# numbers checkable, and it is checkable in the repository. Serving it from the
# site would publish files with no reader and no route into the page.
#
# ⚠️ Every rule is anchored with a leading slash, and tools/check-site.mjs
# rejects one that is not. An unanchored .gitignore rule matches at every
# depth: `data/` also hides `assets/data/`, where the page reads its density
# figures. Wrangler reports nothing for that — the file is simply absent and
# the page 404s at runtime. Measured against workerd, 2026-09-02.
#
# check-site.mjs also fails if a top-level entry appears that is neither part
# of the site nor listed here, so this cannot quietly fall behind.

/*.md
/LICENSE
/.git/
/.github/
/.gitignore
/.wrangler/
/.assetsignore
/wrangler.jsonc
/corpus/
/data/
/docs/
/tests/
/tools/
